      ":question/problem": "![](images/58/5866bffdde1a59974822ddb5f5c1e0c8b959536871593666c9b41e886031198f.png)\n\nLet $g(t)$ denote the population of bears between $1980$ and $1988$ in a certain country, where $t$ is the number of years since the year $1980$. The graph of $y = g^{\u2032}(t)$, the derivative of $y = g(t)$, is given above. In what year did the population reach a relative maximum?"
